   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch5/q1",
   "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:85mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-2-ch5/q01-fig-1.png\" alt=\"Figure 1: polar sketch with pole O, the initial line and the half-line θ = π/2 dashed; the curve C runs from the half-line θ = π/2 down to the initial line, passing through A; N is on the initial line directly below A, and the region R between the curve, AN and the initial line is shaded\"></figure><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> shown in Figure 1 has polar equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=4+\\cos2\\theta\\qquad0\\leqslant\\theta\\leqslant\\frac{\\pi}{2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>At the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac92\"></span></p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\"></span> lies on the initial line and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AN\"></span> is perpendicular to the initial line.</p><p>The finite region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 1, is bounded by the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, the initial line and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AN\"></span>.</p><p>Find the exact area of the shaded region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\\pi+q\\sqrt3\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are rational numbers to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(9)</span></p>",
   "steps": [
