   "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:55mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-2-ch5/q02-fig-1.png\" alt=\"Figure 1: a closed curve around the pole O, roughly circular with a slight inward dent at the bottom, and the initial line drawn from O to the right\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of a curve with polar equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=6+a\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;a&lt;6\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\"></span></p><p>The area enclosed by the curve is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{97\\pi}{2}\"></span></p><p>Find the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(8)</span></p>",
