   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch5/q4",
   "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:115mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-2-ch5/q04-fig-1.png\" alt=\"Figure 1: rectangle ABCD with AB marked 1.2 m; inside it a white closed curve shaped like a figure-of-eight outline pinched at the top and bottom middle; the area between the curve and the rectangle is shaded; labelled &quot;Diagram not to scale&quot;\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the design for a table top in the shape of a rectangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\"></span>. The length of the table, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>, is 1.2 m. The area inside the closed curve is made of glass and the surrounding area, shown shaded in Figure 1, is made of wood.</p><p>The perimeter of the glass is modelled by the curve with polar equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=0.4+a\\cos2\\theta\\qquad0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=0.2\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Hence, given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AD\"></span> = 60 cm,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>find the area of the wooden part of the table top, giving your answer in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm m^2\"></span> to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(8)</span></li></ol>",
