   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch5/q6",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><p>Show on an Argand diagram the locus of points given by the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> satisfying</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|z-4-3\\mathrm i|=5\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li></ol><p>Taking the initial line as the positive real axis with the pole at the origin and given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\in[\\alpha,\\alpha+\\pi]\"></span>,<br>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=-\\arctan\\left(\\frac43\\right)\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\" start=\"2\"><li><p>show that this locus of points can be represented by the polar curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=8\\cos\\theta+6\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol><p>The set of points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=\\left\\{z:0\\leqslant\\arg z\\leqslant\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right\\}\\cap\\{z:|z-4-3\\mathrm i|\\leqslant5\\}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Show, by shading on your Argand diagram, the set of points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</li><li>Find the <strong>exact</strong> area of the region defined by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, giving your answer in simplest form.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li></ol>",
   "steps": [
    "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-2-ch5/q06-ms-p15-1.png\" width=\"900\" height=\"605\" alt=\"PMT mark scheme for Core Pure 2 Ch.5 Polar Coordinates Q6; source page 15, segment 1 of 5. Includes the working, marks, alternative methods and notes in source order.\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:100%\"></figure>",
